4. Overhead weather protection  
   a. Continuous overhead weather protection (i.e., canopies, awnings, marquees, and ar-  
   cades) is required along at least 60 percent of the street frontage of a structure on a principal pedestrian street, except for structures within the Pike/Pine Conservation Overlay District on lots that contain a character structure as provided in Chapter 23.73.  
