25.06.150 Wetlands management

To the maximum extent possible, development shall avoid the short-term and long-term adverse impacts associated with the destruction or modification of wetlands, especially development that limits or disrupts the ability of wetland to alleviate flooding impacts. The floodplain administrators shall implement the following process:

A. Review proposals for development within areas of special flood hazard for their possible impacts on wetlands located within such areas;

B. Ensure that development activities in or around wetlands do not negatively affect public safety, health, and welfare by disrupting the wetland’s ability to reduce flood and storm drainage; and

C. Request technical assistance from the Washington State Department of Ecology in identifying wetland areas.

